The original board is:

\[
\begin{matrix}
\text{shaded} & \text{shaded} & \text{white}\\
\text{white} & \text{shaded} & \text{white}\\
\text{white} & \text{shaded} & \text{white}
\end{matrix}
\]

After a \(90^\circ\) clockwise turn:

- The shaded square in the upper-left moves to the upper-right.
- The vertical shaded column becomes a horizontal shaded middle row.

Thus the rotated board is:

\[
\begin{matrix}
\text{white} & \text{white} & \text{shaded}\\
\text{shaded} & \text{shaded} & \text{shaded}\\
\text{white} & \text{white} & \text{white}
\end{matrix}
\]

This matches Board C.

\[
\boxed{\text{C: Board C}}
\]
